questions.explanation:
Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate \(\sqrt{x+1}+1\):
\[
\frac{\sqrt{x+1}-1}{x}
=
\frac{(\sqrt{x+1}-1)(\sqrt{x+1}+1)}
{x(\sqrt{x+1}+1)}
=
\frac{x+1-1}{x(\sqrt{x+1}+1)}
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{x+1}+1}.
\]
As \(x\to0^+\), \(\sqrt{x+1}\to1\), so the expression tends to \(\frac{1}{1+1}=\frac{1}{2}\).
